    </section>

    <!-- Buyer's Guide -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-8">How to choose swim club management software</h2>
      <div class="space-y-6 text-ink-soft">
        <p>
          Not all club management platforms are built the same. Most were designed for generic sports clubs or for the American market, then awkwardly adapted for UK swimming. Here is what to look for when evaluating swim club management software for your committee:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-8 mt-8">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">1. UK-specific compliance support</h3>
            <p>Your software should understand <a href="/features/compliance/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline">Wavepower safeguarding</a>, DBS tracking, and Swim England membership categories out of the box. American platforms like TeamUnify have no concept of Wavepower or SwimMark accreditation. Generic tools like Spond treat swimming the same as five-a-side football. Look for a platform that tracks DBS expiry dates, coaching qualifications, and safeguarding training automatically.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">2. Direct Debit billing, not just card payments</h3>
            <p>UK swimming clubs collect monthly subscriptions, and <a href="/swimming-club-billing-software/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline">Direct Debit is the standard</a>. Standing orders require parents to set up payments manually and give your treasurer no visibility when someone cancels. Card payments mean higher fees. A proper swim club management system should collect fees via GoCardless Direct Debit automatically, retry failed payments, and give your treasurer a clear dashboard of who has paid and who has not.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">3. Transparent, flat-rate pricing</h3>
            <p>Some platforms charge per member, which means your costs rise as your club grows. SwimClub Manager costs around £649 per year. Others hide pricing behind "request a quote" forms. Look for flat monthly pricing with no per-member surcharges and no annual lock-in. Swimly starts at <a href="/pricing/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline">£29 per month</a> for clubs up to 200 members, and there is a free plan for clubs under 50.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">4. Works on a phone at poolside</h3>
            <p>Coaches take <a href="/features/attendance/" class="text-mint-ink hover:text-[#0F2D2D] underline">attendance at 6am poolside sessions</a>. Parents check schedules between school runs. If your software requires a laptop or a desktop browser, it will not get used where it matters most. Choose a platform that is mobile-first, works on any device, and loads quickly on a phone at the pool.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">5. Easy handover between committee members</h3>
            <p>Volunteer committees change every year or two. When a treasurer steps down, can the next person pick up where they left off? Your software should have role-based access so committee members see exactly what they need, audit trails so nothing gets lost, and a setup simple enough that a new volunteer can get started without training.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">6. Data security and UK hosting</h3>
            <p>You are handling children's personal data, medical information, and payment details. Your platform should be hosted in the UK, encrypted in transit and at rest, and fully GDPR compliant. Avoid platforms that store data in the US or pass it through third-country servers without adequate safeguards.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-8">
          Swimly was designed from the ground up with all six of these criteria in mind. It is the only swim club management platform built specifically for UK clubs by someone who actually sits on a poolside bench at 6am on a Saturday morning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How It Works -->
    <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl text-[#0F2D2D] mb-8">How Swimly works</h2>
      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-3 gap-8">
        <div class="text-center">
          <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full bg-[#85FFC7]/20 border border-[#1F7A52]/15 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-4">
            <span class="text-mint-ink font-semibold text-lg">1</span>
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#0F2D2D] mb-3">Set up your club</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-ink-mute">Import your members from a spreadsheet or start fresh. Configure squads, fee structures, and training sessions. We handle the migration for founding clubs.</p>
